{"title":"Career roadmap · Content Curator","role":"Content Curator","summary":"A Content Curator researches, evaluates, organises and presents useful content for a specific audience or platform. In Digital Humanities and Cultural Studies, this can include cultural archives, digital collections, educational resources, heritage content, research materials, editorial collections and online knowledge platforms.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Digital Humanities / Cultural Studies"},"about":[{"label":"Alignment","text":"Strong direct alignment"}],"intro":[{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"The career can be entered through editorial/content roles, but specialised digital-humanities positions benefit from research methods, metadata, digital archives, data literacy and content-management skills."}]}],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Typical route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BA Digital Humanities/Cultural Studies","Content/Research Internship","Content Researcher / Editorial Assistant","Junior Content Curator","Content Curator","Senior Content Curator","Content Strategy/Editorial Lead","Head of Content / Digital Collections Lead"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build research, cultural studies, writing, digital-content and information-organisation skills."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialise in cultural content, digital archives, education, publishing, heritage or platform content."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Lead content collections, editorial programmes, digital archives and audience-engagement projects."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress toward Content Strategy Lead, Digital Collections Lead, Editorial Director, Knowledge Manager or Digital Humanities Programme Director."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{